{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they struggled.</b> A root meaning breaking, as in 'כי רצץ עזב דלים' and 'וירוצץ אסא'." "<b>If so.</b> The suffering of pregnancy is great — <b>why then am I</b> alive? It would be better for me to die at once and not suffer further the pain of pregnancy and childbirth." "<b>And she went to inquire of YHWH.</b> To inquire of the prophets who were in those days what this is, that they struggle within her; she knew well enough about herself that her days to give birth had not yet been completed, and she was concerned lest she miscarry."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:51.238825472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}